            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0111" n="9" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg9"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 General Committee (Arms)/88:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Delegate</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-01-31T12:00:00-05:00">January 31,
                            1935—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>468. Your No. 969, January 29, 5 p.m. It was our understanding that the amendment
                    of Category V, as suggested in the instruction of December 24,<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d9-f1"/> taken in conjunction with the amended text of Article 30
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">e</hi>) authorized in that instruction provided for
                    the inspection on the spot for production of civil aviation material for which
                    the French contend. Do the French desire something more than this? If so, please
                    submit by telegram, for my consideration, such modifications of the present text
                    of the Draft Articles as would be necessary to carry out their ideas.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
